---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';

const domain = SITE.email.split('@')[1];
---

<PageLayout
  title="Terms & Conditions"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  description={`Terms and conditions for using ${SITE.name}.`}
  lede="The rules for using this website, stated plainly."
  updated="August 29, 2026"
>
  <p>
    By accessing or using {SITE.name} at <strong>{SITE.url}</strong>, you agree to these terms.
    If you do not agree, please do not use the site.
  </p>

  <h2>Use of content</h2>
  <p>
    All content on this site — articles, photographs, graphics and code — is the property of
    {SITE.name} or its licensors. You may read, share links to, and quote short excerpts (with
    attribution and a link back) for personal, non-commercial purposes. You may not reproduce
    entire articles, scrape the site, or republish content without written permission.
  </p>

  <h2>No professional advice</h2>
  <p>
    Content on {SITE.name} is for informational and inspirational purposes only. Nothing here
    constitutes professional design, structural, legal, financial or safety advice. Always consult
    a qualified professional before undertaking building work or making significant financial
    decisions.
  </p>

  <h2>Affiliate links and advertising</h2>
  <p>
    Some links are affiliate links and some pages carry advertising. See our
    <a href="/disclosure/">disclosure policy</a> for full details. We are not responsible for the
    content, pricing or availability of third-party websites we link to.
  </p>

  <h2>User conduct</h2>
  <p>You agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Use the site for any unlawful purpose.</li>
    <li>Attempt to gain unauthorised access to any part of the site or its infrastructure.</li>
    <li>Transmit spam, malware or any harmful code.</li>
    <li>Misrepresent your identity or affiliation when contacting us.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent permitted by law, {SITE.name} is not liable for any direct, indirect,
    incidental or consequential loss arising from your use of, or inability to use, this site or
    any content on it.
  </p>

  <h2>External links</h2>
  <p>
    We link to third-party sites for convenience and reference. We do not control those sites and
    are not responsible for their content, privacy practices or availability.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms at any time. Continued use of the site after changes are posted
    constitutes acceptance of the revised terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of the jurisdiction in which {SITE.name} is registered.
    Any disputes will be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of that jurisdiction.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <hr />
  <p>
    <em>
      This template is a starting point, not legal advice. Have a solicitor or attorney review it
      for your jurisdiction before you launch.
    </em>
  </p>
</PageLayout>
